{"name":"Bleached Olive","hex":"#55bb88","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bleached","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Whitened; made white using bleach","Faded or washed out by weather and strong sunlight."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of bleach"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bleached"},{"term":"olive","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tree of species Olea europaea cultivated since ancient times in the Mediterranean for its fruit and the oil obtained from it.","The small oval fruit of this tree, eaten ripe (usually black) or unripe (usually green)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a grayish green color, that of an unripe olive."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/olive"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bleached","blocks":[{"text":"Bleached is an American pop band consisting of sisters Jennifer and Jessica Clavin, formerly of Mika Miko. The band plays a style of rock, pop, rock and roll, and indie rock. Bleached was established in Los Angeles in 2011. The group has released three studio albums, Ride Your Heart (2013), Welcome the Worms (2016) and Don't You Think You've Had Enough? (2019), all with Dead Oceans, and have charted on the Billboard charts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Bleached_performing_at_The_Great_Escape%2C_May_2016.jpg/330px-Bleached_performing_at_The_Great_Escape%2C_May_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bleached","wikidata":"Q25056076"},{"title":"Olive","blocks":[{"text":"The cultivated olive is a subspecies of subtropical evergreen tree in the family Oleaceae. Modern cultivars are traced primarily to the Near East, Aegean Sea, and Strait of Gibraltar. Olea europaea is the type species for its genus, Olea, which lends its name to the Oleaceae plant family. The olive fruit is classed botanically as a drupe, similar in structure and function to the cherry or peach. The term oil was originally synonymous with olive oil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Olivesfromjordan.jpg/330px-Olivesfromjordan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olive","wikidata":"Q1621080"},{"title":"Olive (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Olive, also called olive green, is a dark shade of yellowish green, like that of unripe or green olives."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Olives_stuffed_with_almonds.jpg/330px-Olives_stuffed_with_almonds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olive_(color)","wikidata":"Q864152"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Bleached_at_Tufnell_Park_Dome%2C_October_2013.jpg/500px-Bleached_at_Tufnell_Park_Dome%2C_October_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Bleached_at_Tufnell_Park_Dome%2C_October_2013.jpg/1280px-Bleached_at_Tufnell_Park_Dome%2C_October_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Bleached_at_Tufnell_Park_Dome%2C_October_2013.jpg/500px-Bleached_at_Tufnell_Park_Dome%2C_October_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bleached performing in London in 2013","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABleached_at_Tufnell_Park_Dome%2C_October_2013.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Jennifer_Clavin_of_Bleached_at_The_Great_Escape%2C_May_2016_%282%29.jpg/500px-Jennifer_Clavin_of_Bleached_at_The_Great_Escape%2C_May_2016_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki